# A player's ALIAS attribute is its alias list, and the player list follows it (#1499): every way
# of writing ALIAS updates what *name, page and lookups find, and alias()/fullalias() read it back.
# Aliases here are never a prefix of a connected player's name, so a miss is a miss and not
# visible_short_page's partial match of who is online.
::case alias.set  @alias makes the player findable by the alias
::login alice Alice alicepass
::login bob Bob bobpass
::as alice
@alias me=Wonder
think [alias(me)]/[fullalias(me)]/[get(me/ALIAS)]
think [strmatch(num(*Wonder),num(me))] [strmatch(num(*wonder),num(me))]
::as bob
page Wonder=Are you Alice?
think [name(*Wonder)]

::case alias.multiple  several aliases, the short alias, too many, an empty one
::as alice
&ALIAS me=Wonder;Dreamer
think [alias(me)]/[fullalias(me)]
think [strmatch(num(*Dreamer),num(me))]
&ALIAS me=Wa;Wb;Wc;Wd
think [get(me/ALIAS)]
&ALIAS me=Wonder;;Dreamer
think [get(me/ALIAS)]

::case alias.taken  an alias another player's name or alias holds is refused
::as bob
@alias me=Alice
@alias me=Dreamer
@alias me=WONDER
think [get(me/ALIAS)]
@alias me=Builder
::as alice
@alias me=builder
@name me=Builder
think [name(me)] [get(me/ALIAS)]
::as bob
@alias me

::case alias.case  a player may recase their own alias
::as alice
@alias me=WONDER;dreamer
think [fullalias(me)]

::case alias.set-forms  @set and alias() write it too
@set me=ALIAS:Rabbit
think [strmatch(num(*Rabbit),num(me))] [strmatch(num(*Wonder),#-1*)]
think [alias(me,Hatter)]
think [alias(me)] [strmatch(num(*Rabbit),#-1*)]

::case alias.clear  clearing it removes the alias from lookups
@alias me
think [strmatch(num(*Hatter),#-1*)]/[alias(me)]/[hasattr(me,ALIAS)]
@alias me=Hatter
&ALIAS me=
think [get(me/ALIAS)]
&ALIAS me
think [strmatch(num(*Hatter),#-1*)]/[hasattr(me,ALIAS)]

::case alias.name  @name with an alias list
@name me=Alice;Queen;Knave
think [fullalias(me)] [strmatch(num(*Knave),num(me))]
@name me=Alice;
think [hasattr(me,ALIAS)] [strmatch(num(*Knave),#-1*)]
@name me=Alice;Qa;Qb;Qc
@name me=Alice;Bob
think [name(me)] [hasattr(me,ALIAS)]

::case alias.rename  renaming to one's own alias, and back
@alias me=Duchess
@name me=Duchess
think [name(me)] [strmatch(num(*Duchess),num(me))]
@name me=Alice
think [name(me)] [strmatch(num(*Duchess),num(me))] [fullalias(me)]
@alias me

::case alias.partial  *name falls back to a unique prefix of a connected player's name (#1502)
::as bob
think [strmatch(num(*Ali),num(*Alice))] [strmatch(num(*ali),num(*Alice))] [name(*Ali)]
